# REQUIRES: python-api
# The frames of an evaluation inside one activation of the evaluator's
# program (D[frames-activation], docs/python-frames.md) on the CPU, in
# double and mixed precision, Inputs/python_frames.py: what a frame gives
# does not depend on the call it is in, on the frames before it, on a frame
# that failed before it, or on what other simulations do in between, to
# the bit; it is what the gradient() and the state of a sampler in the
# order of the input give, to the bit, and what a simulation in the spatial
# order gives within the rounding of sums in another order.
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_frames.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide activation CPU Double | FileCheck %s -DMODE="CPU Double"
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_frames.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide activation CPU Mixed | FileCheck %s -DMODE="CPU Mixed"
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: 6 frames against the gradient() and the state of a sampler in the order of the input, equal to the bit: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: against a simulation in the spatial order compiled from the frame: the energy {{.*}} kJ/mol (tolerance {{.*}}), the rows {{.*}} relative (tolerance {{.*}}): True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: one frame per call: True; frames that repeat and frames far apart in one call: True; batches of two frames: True; 120 frames in one call: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: with the calls of a second evaluator and the steps of a sampler in between: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: after a frame that fails in the middle of a call, one that fails as the first of an activation, and frames that are refused: True
# CHECK: [[MODE]]: at other values of a tunable the energies change, and at the first values again they are those of before: True
# CHECK: activation passed
